# Ship the Proton Mail web-composer handoff

## Goal

Provide an immediately useful Free-plan composition path that does not depend on
Bridge, provider client registration, or mailbox authority.

## Completed work

- Verified the pinned WebClients `mailto:` protocol-handler path and field
  parser.
- Added `protonmail-ai mail compose-url` for To, Cc, Bcc, subject, and body.
- Preserved tagged aliases, Unicode text, and line breaks through the two
  required percent-encoding layers.
- Added `--body-file` so long message text need not be supplied as a process
  argument.
- Kept the command side-effect free: it emits text only and does not open a
  browser or send mail.
- Classified the implementation as fact-informed by pinned WebClients source.

## Acceptance evidence

- `web-compose-handoff` integration target exercises the built binary.
- Nine synthetic process tests cover valid encoding and fail-closed input.
- Repository provenance validation covers the new implementation and tests.
- `docs/architecture/web-compose-handoff.mdc` records the pinned provider
  behavior and privacy boundary.
